.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ckman-config-ndef-write 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-config\-ndef\-write \- Replace the NDEF message with the file contents (\*(Aq\-\*(Aq for stdin)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-config\-ndef\-write\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Replace the NDEF message with the file contents (\*(Aq\-\*(Aq for stdin).
.PP
The write is crash\-consistent: a crash or unplug mid\-write leaves an empty message rather than a partially written one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
File containing the NDEF message (\*(Aq\-\*(Aq for stdin, empty to clear)
